>     TESTING-ONLY: enable X86_5LEVEL by default

Okay, I can confim this.

The problem is that with X86_5LEVEL enabled, 512m of RAM is not enough.
sparse_init() tries and fails to allocate 256M of memory using
memblock_virt_alloc().

Looks like we need to find a way to make NR_MEM_SECTIONS dynamic. But it's
tricky.

Dave, any chance you could help me with this?

